# Binary game data and assets must NEVER get line-ending conversion. Without
# this, a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true injects \r bytes into these
# binary files, corrupting them - e.g. a .map then fails ZMap::Read and the
# engine falls back to its featureless random map. (macOS/Linux were unaffected,
# so this was a Windows-only "garbage map" bug.)
*.map       binary
*.bmp       binary
*.png       binary
*.ico       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.wav       binary
*.ogg       binary
*.mid       binary
*.tileinfo  binary
*.xcf       binary
*.icescene  binary
*.rar       binary
*.zip       binary
*.db        binary
*.o         binary
*.LST       binary
*.MID       binary

# Source files are stored CRLF in this repo and compile fine on every platform;
# leave their endings ALONE (-text) so git never tries to renormalize them
# (forcing eol here made every source file show as modified). Only the binary
# rules above matter for the Windows corruption bug.
*.cpp  -text
*.h    -text
*.txt  -text
*.md   -text
